% The rule limit counts the rules the rewrite keeps, not the rules the search
% for its adornments reads.  p's rule is written four times and the draft
% keeps one copy, so the rewrite of this query generates three rules -- the
% seed recording q's binding, q$bf's rule and p$ff's copy of p's -- and fits a
% limit of three, though the search reads q's rule and all four of p's.

e(a, b).
e(b, c).
f(a, x).

p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
q(X, Y) :- f(X, Y).

p(X, Y), q(a, Z)?
